.TH ADSCUTTER 1 "" "AdsCutter @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adscutter \- cut ads out of TV recordings without re\-encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adscutter
.RB [ \-v ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AdsCutter
is a desktop application that removes advertising breaks from DVB\-T/T2
television recordings.
It reads MPEG transport streams and Matroska files and writes Matroska,
copying the streams without re\-encoding.
.PP
Every kept segment starts on a frame where decoding can begin and may end on
any frame.
H.264 and HEVC cut points are rewritten so that each segment starts cleanly.
.PP
Ad detection (fades to black, separators, and regions of the picture drawn by
the user, such as the text under a channel logo) is built in and only runs
when asked for from the
.B Analysis
which is then disabled.
It proposes a cut list that can be reviewed and edited before export.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print FFmpeg diagnostics.
Broadcast recordings start mid\-stream, so expect warnings about missing
references.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.I file
Recording to open.
A file can also be dropped on the window; a cut list dropped on an open
recording is loaded.
.PP
Qt options such as
.B \-platform
are accepted as well.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ADSCUTTER_HWDEC
Hardware decoding:
.BR auto " (Vulkan, then VAAPI, then software),"
.BR vulkan ,
.BR vaapi ,
or
.BR none .
Overrides
.BR View " > " "Hardware Decoding" ,
which is then disabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB name .adscutter.json
The cut list, saved next to the recording
.IR name .ts
or
.IR name .mkv .
.TP
.IB name .cut.mkv
Default name of the exported recording.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/adscutter/
Packet indexes and analysis results, keyed by the recording's path, size and
modification time.
Safe to delete; they are rebuilt when needed.
Honours
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME .
.TP
.I ~/.config/adscutter/AdsCutter.conf
Preferences, recent files and region presets.
Honours
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.SH NOTES
The keyboard shortcuts are listed under
.BR Help " > " "Keyboard Shortcuts" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR mkvmerge (1)
